ISO timestamp to localized date in web app:

```javascript
// JavaScript/React
const isoTimestamp = "2026-11-23T14:30:00Z";

// Option 1: Intl.DateTimeFormat (best for localization)
const date = new Date(isoTimestamp);
const formatted = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', {
  month: 'short',
  day: 'numeric',
  year: 'numeric'
}).format(date);
console.log(formatted); // "Nov 23, 2026"

// Option 2: toLocaleDateString (simpler but less control)
const formatted2 = new Date(isoTimestamp).toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
  month: 'short',
  day: 'numeric',
  year: 'numeric'
});

// React component
function ApiTimestamp({ isoTime }) {
  return (
    <span>
      {new Date(isoTime).toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
        month: 'short',
        day: 'numeric',
        year: 'numeric'
      })}
    </span>
  );
}

// Usage: <ApiTimestamp isoTime="2026-11-23T14:30:00Z" />
```

**Option 1** (Intl) better for locale-aware apps (swap `'en-US'` for user's locale). **Option 2** shorter for fixed locale. For timezones, parse before format or use library (date-fns, Day.js).
